{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>We are all sons of one man.</b> It is possible to explain this argument as follows: they said — because we are brothers, sons of one man, and we do not separate one from another, for such is our father's will, we have all come together as one to purchase food, and we did not send one of us with his servants. And so the matter was, for why would he send all of them? Rather, it is because they did not wish to separate one from another. It is also possible that they did so on account of the severity of the famine, so that they would not rob their servants on the road of the grain that they would bring. And it is possible that they said to him, \"We are all sons of one man\" — you can investigate him, for he is known in the gates for the honor of his wealth and the multitude of his sons, and if you ask and investigate you will know that we are truthful and righteous men, sons of a righteous man, and not spies." "And the sense of <b>Your servants are not spies</b> is that we are truthful from our youth in all our matters — your servants have not been spies from then until now. And likewise (Genesis 42:31), \"We were not spies\" — ever. Now our Rabbis were prompted, as I have mentioned, and interpreted (Genesis Rabbah 91:6) that they entered through ten gates, in the manner of spies, and therefore he framed the accusation against them. And this is a valid argument, but Scripture did not mention it. Moreover, they said to him at the outset, \"We are all sons of one man,\" which is itself what obligates them. And it is possible that at first he said to them: You entered through ten gates, and now you are gathered in one place and joined together — this is nothing but the way of spies. And they said to him: Because we are brothers, we assembled together. And he said to them, <b>No, but to see the nakedness of the land you have come</b> — for if you are brothers, you should have entered through one gate, as you are now together. Then they said that the one is not with them, and they went to seek him. And Scripture does not bother to elaborate on the reasoning behind the arguments."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:01.215944240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}